e occurs when the library verifies a General JSON Serialization JWS using a set of keys. Due to a coding error, the library fails to correctly identify the specific key ID (kid) and may instead accept a signature made by any valid key in the set. This can allow an attacker with a valid key to bypass authorization checks in applications that rely on the key ID to identify specific tenants or users.","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"a flaw was found in the jwcrypto library, which is used for implementing javascript object signing and encryption (jose) standards. the issue occurs when the library verifies a general json serialization jws using a set of keys. due to a coding error, the library fails to correctly identify the specific key id (kid) and may instead accept a signature made by any valid key in the set. this can allow an attacker with a valid key to bypass authorization checks in applications that rely on the key id to identify specific tenants or users."},{"subject":"CVE-2026-84185","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform 2","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat ansible automation platform 2"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-84185","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 10","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat enterprise linux 10"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-84185","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 7","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat enterprise linux 7"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-84185","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat enterprise linux 8"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-84185","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat enterprise linux 9"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-84185","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat OpenShift AI (RHOAI)","source"